diff --git a/crates/rightkit-agents/CHANGELOG.md b/crates/rightkit-agents/CHANGELOG.md
index 4c4cd8d..82e7ff5 100644
--- a/crates/rightkit-agents/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/crates/rightkit-agents/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,5 +1,23 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## 0.3.0 (unreleased)
+
+Closes the open rightkit-agents gaps of the CodeRight and Pulse ports (#419, #567, #573, #695, #704, #705, #706, #707). Nothing in this release was compiled or run when written; CI is the first compile.
+
+- Breaking: `rate_limit::RateLimitState` rules now follow CodeRight's pinned tests (#707). `probe_failed` leaves `Unsupported` untouched (it used to replace it with `ProbeFailed`), and `mark_unsupported` overwrites a known snapshot (it used to keep it). `mark_unsupported_if_unknown` keeps the 0.2.0 rule. `observe` still wins over every earlier state. `RateLimitSnapshot` is now its own struct (it was an alias of `RateLimitInfo`) with `From` conversions both ways, and `observe` accepts either; `snapshot()` returns `&RateLimitSnapshot`. `RateLimitState` and `RateLimitSnapshot` implement `Serialize` and `Deserialize` as camelCase tagged JSON (`{"state":"probeFailed","message":"..","lastKnown":{..}}`). `RateLimitInfo` and the `AgentEvent` JSON are unchanged.
+- Breaking (behavior): `discovery::find_binaries` and `find_binary` skip empty and relative `PATH` entries (#704). An empty entry (`PATH=/usr/bin::/bin`) used to resolve against the current directory, so a CLI planted in the working directory was found and run. New `discovery::find_binaries_in(name, search_path)` is the same search over an explicit path; a name that is empty or holds a path separator finds nothing.
+- `discovery::run_bounded_with` and `discovery::probe_with` take a `CommandCustomiser` (`&dyn Fn(&mut Command)`) applied to the probe process before it starts, so a host can run `--version` and `auth status` probes through its own confinement instead of unsandboxed (#704). `run_bounded` and `probe` keep their behavior.
+- New module `launch_env` (#705, #567, #573): `BYOK_ENV_VARS` now also names the Bedrock, Vertex, AWS, Google, OpenAI base-URL/org/project, xAI, Cursor, OpenRouter, MiniMax and TinyFish variables CodeRight scrubs (CodeRight's own daemon and gateway secrets stay with that app: pass them to `scrub`). Breaking (behavior): `SessionConfig::scrub_byok_env` removes the longer list. `LaunchEnv { remove, set }` with `scrub_byok`, `scrub(names)` (a caller-supplied list), `with_var`, `merge` and `apply(&mut Command)`; its `Debug` prints variable names, never values. `session::BYOK_ENV_VARS` is re-exported from the new home.
+- `session::SessionConfig::scrub_env(names)` (caller-supplied scrub list) and `with_launch_env(LaunchEnv)` (#705, #567, #573).
+- `claude::ClaudeAccountEnv::{OAuthToken, ApiKey}` and `claude::launch_env(Option<&ClaudeAccountEnv>)` (#567): scrubs the credential-class variables, then sets exactly one of `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` or the API-key variable. `Debug` redacts the secret.
+- `claude::ClaudeExtras::mcp_config` and `strict_mcp_config` (#567, #705): `--strict-mcp-config` and `--mcp-config <json or path>` on the argv, validated (non-empty, no NUL, strict needs a config). This is argv pass-through only; the crate still speaks no MCP. `tests/scope.rs` no longer lists the two flag names as forbidden tokens; it pins them to `claude.rs` instead (`mcp_flags_are_only_argv_pass_through`). The scope change needs the owner's confirmation.
+- `codex::CodexExtras { config_overrides, strict_config }`, `codex::build_args_with`, `codex::mcp_server_overrides(name, command, args)`, `codex::toml_string` and `codex::account_env(codex_home)` (#573): `-c key=value` overrides before `app-server` (a scoped MCP server for one launch is `-c mcp_servers.<name>.command=..` and `.args=..`, nothing written to Codex's config file), `--strict-config`, and a launch environment that scrubs credentials and pins `CODEX_HOME`. `session::SessionExtras::codex` carries them. The usage-limit event (`AgentEvent::RateLimit` with status `rejected` and `resets_at`) and fail-closed unknown methods were already in 0.2.0.
+- Claude control channel and parser, aligned with CodeRight's contracts (#706). `claude::next_request_id_with_prefix(prefix, kind)` and `REQUEST_ID_PREFIX`: a host keeps `coderight-<kind>-<n>`, and the counter is shared. `interrupt_request`, `initialize_request`, `set_model_request` and `set_permission_mode_request` return the frame as a `serde_json::Value` with no newline (the `*_frame` functions add it). `parse_control_response_strict` returns a typed `ControlResponseError` (`MissingResponse`, `MissingRequestId`, `UnknownSubtype`) where `parse_control_response` returns `None`. Breaking (behavior): a malformed `control_response` is now `AgentEvent::Unknown` leniently (it was dropped) and a `ParseError` under `UnknownPolicy::FailClosed`. Breaking: `ClaudeAccountIdentity` gains `subscription_type`, `token_source` and `api_key_source` and is read from the Agent SDK's `account` object (the older `accountInfo` is the fallback), and `InterruptReceipt` gains `pending_messages` (the queued messages themselves, for re-queueing) next to the count; struct literals of either no longer compile. `UnknownPolicy::FailClosed` now treats a payload key with a `null` value as absent (it used to count it as present) and also refuses a `system` message with no `subtype`, a `system/init` with no `session_id`, and a malformed `control_response`; lenient parsing still defaults those to empty. `claude::AnswerOutcome` and `claude::decide(request, outcome)` give an async host the same fail-closed mapping as `answer_can_use_tool` (no responder and timeout both deny with `NO_ANSWER_MESSAGE`), so its responder can use its own timer with `DEFAULT_PERMISSION_TIMEOUT`.
+- New `AgentEvent::ApprovalContext { id, tool_use_id, agent_id, blocked_path }` (#571), emitted right after the Claude `ApprovalRequested` with the same id when the `can_use_tool` request carried any of the three. `ApprovalRequested` keeps its fields so existing patterns compile. The wire placement of the three keys is unverified.
+- `session::Session::spawn_with(config, launcher)` (#695): the session builds the `Command` and hands it to a launcher `FnOnce(&mut Command) -> io::Result<SpawnedChild>`, which starts the process however the host requires (confinement, ACL leases, a job, a wrapper) and returns it with its pipes. `SpawnedChild::from_owned`, `from_std` and `from_parts` (a host `ChildHandle`: `id`, `try_wait`, `wait_then_kill`, plus any reader and writer for the pipes). The crate keeps the protocol handling; the process stays the host's. On a failed startup the handle is told to stop the process before the error returns. `Session::spawn` is `spawn_with` over `OwnedCommand`, unchanged in behavior. `Session::try_pid` returns `None` when a custom handle does not know its pid (`pid()` returns `0` then). `session::SessionExtras::unknown_policy` now also applies to Claude sessions: a refused line is reported as `SessionEvent::Error` and not forwarded. An async twin of `Session` is not part of this release.
+- New feature `logs` and module `logs` (#419): `discover_open(home)`, `discover_in(claude_dir, codex_dir)`, `default_claude_dir`, `default_codex_dir` (honor `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` and `CODEX_HOME`), `LogParser` (Claude Code and Codex rows to `AgentEvent`, with the session id, cwd, model, timestamps and best title in `SessionMeta`), `LogTail` (incremental, complete lines only, 1-based contiguous `seq`), `read_log`, `read_meta`. Sidechain rows, `isMeta` rows and injected context are not events; per-row usage is not emitted (the CLIs repeat it). New `AgentEvent::UserMessage { text }` carries user messages read from a log. Lifted from the Pulse membrane transcript adapters; the `custom-title`, `ai-title` and Codex `compacted` rows are unverified.
+- New feature `external` and module `external` (#419 follow-up): `ExternalSessions::{list, history, tail, deliver}` over `ExternalConfig`. `list` returns `ExternalSession { id, title, cwd, host, account, status, liveness, input_available, updated_at }` (ids `claude:<id>` and `codex:<id>`) from Claude Code's live-session registry (`<claude dir>/sessions/*.json`, checked against the process table) plus recent logs. `history(id, after_seq, limit)` pages `(seq, AgentEvent)`. `tail(id, after_seq)` returns a `Tail` (a `Receiver` wrapper whose drop stops the polling thread; `receiver()` exposes the receiver) and answers `NotRunning` for a chat that is not running. `deliver(id, text, deadline)` returns a `DeliveryReceipt { state, msg_id, unproven }` through a host-installed `Deliverer`, because this crate does not know how a Claude Code build accepts outside input (`Unsupported` without one). Codex has no registry, so Codex sessions list with `Unknown` liveness and `tail` and `deliver` answer `Unsupported`. Errors are `NotFound`, `NotRunning`, `Unsupported`, `Other`. The registry key names are unverified against a recorded registry.
+
 ## 0.2.0 (2026-10-17)
 
 - `discovery::run_bounded` uses `rightkit-child-process` in every feature configuration for whole-tree termination & native output readers that cancel & join after a bounded drain window. Each stream retains at most `discovery::PROBE_OUTPUT_CAP` (64 KiB); descendants retaining pipe writers cannot leave drain threads behind. Dependency minimum is `rightkit-child-process` 0.5.1.
